 "_comment": [
  "FACTORtv — NATIONALITIES.",
  "",
  "The second of the three identity fields a player gets (name, nationality,",
  "home circuit — see HANDOVER). It exists for ONE reason and it is worth",
  "stating so the list never grows into a questionnaire: every field a player",
  "fills in has to be something the booth can say TRUTHFULLY and",
  "INTERESTINGLY. A favourite colour is neither. A nationality is both —",
  "'the young Australian, and this is his home race' earns its keep on the",
  "first lap of a season.",
  "",
  "`country` MUST MATCH THE SPELLING IN tracks.json, because that is what a",
  "home race is compared against. The comparison folds a leading 'the' (the",
  "circuit data holds both 'United States' and 'the United States'), so the",
  "article here is only for how it reads in a sentence.",
  "",
  "`demonym` is used as a bare noun after an article — 'the young {demonym}' —",
  "so it carries no article of its own and is always capitalised.",
  "",
  "ORDERED BY HOW LIKELY A PLAYER IS TO PICK IT, not alphabetically: this list",
  "is scrolled with a mouse in an overlay while a game waits."
 ],

